Immortal Redneck is mix of this type of games:
*Ziggurat - similar mechanics, randomly generate levels (every run is different) and characters with different abbilities, challange rooms (not taken any damage, speedrun, reach the chest with  treasure, etc), good and bad scrolls which can you help or not, my favourite scrolls are gravity like in mars, you can find items in vasses (they are everywhere) or realoading weapons in inventory but if you dont have luck you can get scrolls with bad effects which makes your game harder;
*Serious Sam series -  fighting in pyramids in ancient egypth with mummies, curses etc, secrets;
*Rogue legacy - receiving gold from enemies and treasures for upgrade your heroes, every death is permament, no checkpoints (but you can still leave the game and resume it in other time);
*Doom - this game is also fast-peaced FPS with many oldschool things like rocket launcher, double jumping or fast switching weapon for do many combos also you can grab ledge and climbing;
*Dark Souls - dying is a part of this game but without feeling is unfair or pointless death. Every run makes your character stronger and you gain skills to beat enemies faster and with better style, first thing you should learn in immortal redneck is how to enemies attack you and how you can avoid unnecessary damage.
Pros:
- This game is huge, content in this game could be spread over 20 dlc;
- Many weapons which enforce a different style of play. In weapons you can reach is crowbar from half-life, rocket launcher from quake 3 arena, ak47 from counter strike, The Noisy Cricket, little gun with powerfull shoots from Man in Black movie;
- Many beatiful levels, every chamber is detailed and thought for beating one chapter (in this game is a pyramid), you need past and survive 6 floors with +/- 10 stunning chambers on every floor;
- Three chapters (pyramids) with different enemies and art style of levels. First pyramid is In the climates of ancient, second steampunk, the third is future/ufo;
- Feeling of shooting and full control of your character and aim. I am a FPS player but never have that much fun from shooting like in this game!
- Bosses and different style of enemies attack;
- Daily and monthly challanges;
- Devs with community constantly doing this game better;
- Many characters (9) and abbilites you can upgrade in three of skills;
- Every character you can play have different statics, passive and active skill. Also every character have 3 different weapons on start (apis have even four);
- Music and sound design;
- Price/quality;
- Beatiful graphics and sound desing;
- Optimization;
- Very hard on start but with experience and upgrades it will be easier for you;
- ADDICTIVE it is really hard get addicted of game when you have that many games like me.
Cons:
- Nothing big.
Verdict:
This is AAA game with many indie mechanics. On of best game I ever played.
