This game was on my wishlist and when I saw it was less than £1 I snapped it up. Had I paid more for it I would have been severely disappointed. It's not that the game is bad, it's just increibly annoying;
The controls are painful. Sometimes the back arrow means walk backwards and sometimes it means turn 180 degrees which made navigating a complete pain. The voice acting wasn't great and didn't make me feel anything for the character (he sounded bored)
Had the game mechanics of movement been easier, the game would have taken half the time to complete as more often than not I went the wrong way. I've just started chapter 2, but don't know if I'll bother finishing at as it's just infuriating. The graphics are fine, the story is fine, it's just not enough to make me put up with the bleeping controls.
UPDATE;
Finished the game. It wasn't worth it.

